          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "I. Hilbert Spaces"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.127,
            0.099,
            0.868,
            0.137
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "ProoF. By the mean value property, if "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "0 < t \\leqslant r,f(a) = (1/2\\pi)\\int_{-\\pi}^{\\pi} f(a + te^{i\\theta})d\\theta."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Hence"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.244,
            0.143,
            0.749,
            0.24
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_20_equation_3.jpg",
          "content": "\\begin{align*}\\left( \\pi r^{2} \\right)^{-1} \\int_{B(a;r)}^{r} f = & \\left( \\pi r^{2} \\right)^{-1} \\int_{0}^{r} t \\left[ \\int_{-\\pi}^{\\pi} f(a + t e^{i \\theta}) d \\theta \\right] dt \\\\= & \\left( 2 / r^{2} \\right) \\int_{0}^{r} t f(a) dt = f(a).\\end{align*}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.125,
            0.265,
            0.736,
            0.286
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1.12. Corollary. "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "If f \\in L_{a}^{2}(G), a \\in G"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "0 < r < \\mathrm{dist}(a, \\partial G)"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " then"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.399,
            0.294,
            0.595,
            0.34
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_20_equation_5.jpg",
          "content": "| f ( a ) | \\leqslant \\frac { 1 } { r \\sqrt { \\pi } } \\| f \\| _ { 2 } ."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.125,
            0.346,
            0.848,
            0.367
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "PROOF. Since "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\bar { B } ( a ; r ) \\subseteq G ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , the preceding lemma and the CBS inequality imply"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.286,
            0.372,
            0.717,
            0.513
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_20_equation_7.jpg",
          "content": "\\begin{align*}|f(a)| = & \\frac{1}{\\pi r^2} \\left| \\int_{B(a;r)} f \\cdot 1 \\right| \\\\\\leqslant & \\frac{1}{\\pi r^2} \\left[ \\int_{B(a;r)} |f|^2 \\right]^{1/2} \\left[ \\int_{B(a;r)} 1^2 \\right]^{1/2} \\\\\\leqslant & \\frac{1}{\\pi r^2} \\parallel f \\parallel_2 r \\sqrt{\\pi}.\\end{align*}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.126,
            0.544,
            0.547,
            0.563
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1.13. Proposition. "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "L _ { a } ^ { 2 } ( G )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is a Hilbert space."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.125,
            0.571,
            0.868,
            0.626
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "PROOF. If "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mu ="
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " area measure on "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "G ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " then "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "L ^ { 2 } ( \\mu )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is a Hilbert space and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "L _ { a } ^ { 2 } ( G ) \\subseteq L ^ { 2 } ( \\mu )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . So it suffices to show that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "L _ { a } ^ { 2 } ( G )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is closed in "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "L ^ { 2 } ( \\mu )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Let "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\{ f _ { n } \\}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " be a sequence in "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "L _ { a } ^ { 2 } ( G )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and let "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "f   \\in   L ^ { 2 } ( \\mu )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " such that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\int | f _ { n } - f | ^ { 2 }   d \\mu \\to 0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " as "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "n   \\to   \\infty"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.124,
            0.626,
            0.871,
            0.775
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Suppose "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\tilde { B } ( a ; r ) \\subseteq G"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and let "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "0 < \\rho < \\mathrm { d i s t } ( B ( a ; r ) , \\partial G )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . By the preceding corollary there is a constant C such that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "| f _ { n } ( z ) - f _ { m } ( z ) | \\leqslant C \\| f _ { n } - f _ { m } \\| _ { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " for all "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "n ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " m and for "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "| z - a | \\leqslant \\rho ."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Thus "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\{ f _ { n } \\}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is a uniformly Cauchy sequence on any closed disk in G. By standard results from analytic function theory (Montel's Theorem or Morera's Theorem, for example), there is an analytic function g on G such that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "f _ { n } ( z ) \\to g ( z )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " uniformly on compact subsets of G. But since "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\int | f _ { n } - f | ^ { 2 }   d \\mu \\to 0 ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " a result of Riesz implies there is a subsequence "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\{ f _ { n _ { k } } \\}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " such that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "f _ { n _ { k } } ( z ) \\to f ( z ) \\mathrm { ~ a . e . ~ } [ \\mu ]"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Thus "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "f = g \\mathrm { a . e . } [ \\mu ]"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and so "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "f   \\in   \\bar { L _ { a } ^ { 2 } ( G ) }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.791,
            0.233,
            0.807
          ],
          "content": [
